.TH __EVENT_LOOP_DESTROY 3 "2026-07-12" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
__event_loop_destroy \- destroy an event_loop (internal function)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cthreadcomm.h>

void __event_loop_destroy(event_loop loop);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Calls event_loop_shutdown() if the caller skipped it (guaranteeing every
reactor thread is joined and no dispatch can be in flight before the
next step), then frees every remaining registration through the same
per-registration path event_loop_remove() uses.

For queue-backed registrations this correctly unlinks each one from its
queue's own waiter list before freeing it, so a queue that outlives this
event_loop is never left with a dangling waiter pointer.  fd
registrations are not closed and queues are not destroyed; only the
event_loop's own registration bookkeeping is freed.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
loop  event_loop to destroy.
.fi
.SH WARNINGS
.nf
Do not call directly; use the event_loop_destroy() macro instead, which
also sets the caller's handle to NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR event_loop_destroy (3),
.BR event_loop_shutdown (3),
.BR event_loop_remove (3)
